> 3.  What mythos does the Grayswandir come from?

First off, it's not a 'the'... just Grayswandir.  It's the personal sword
  of Corwin, Prince of Amber, from Roger Zelazny's CHRONICLES OF AMBER
  fantasy novels.  It was forged by moonlight, at the base of a stairway
  leading to a dream-realm in the sky that only appears by the light of
  the full moon.  It's engraved with a portion of the Pattern, a magical
  design.  (It has a companion blade, by the way - the sword used by
  Corwin's brother Bleys, which is golden instead of silvery but other-
  wise identical.)

For more details, read the books.  Grayswandir's powers are mostly due
  to it being charged with the power of the Pattern, which makes it
  very effective against creatures of Chaos - they tended to burst 
  into flame when wounded by it.  

